{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhsW3qJy8oCYpnRRCe9m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate, `designed_exemplar_similarity`, and it passes the self-check (`OK`). That check doesn't test novelty or convergence, and it may not fit well: its smoke-fit ELPD-LOO was −1277.6, against −1003.0 for the current best model. That number comes from a 100-draw, single-chain smoke fit, so the full admission fit will tell for sure.\n\n**Hypothesis (exemplar account):** people remember a few examples of \"designed\" coin sequences:\n- **Streaks:** HHHH…, TTTT…\n- **Perfect alternation:** HTHT…, THTH…\n- **Repeated short patterns:** HHT, HTT and HHTT repeated, counted only when the sequence is long enough to show a pattern repeating.\n\nA sequence looks random to the extent it is unlike all of them. Similarity to each example falls off exponentially with the number of flips where the two differ. It is summed over the examples, so the closest ones dominate, and compared against a fitted constant baseline. The sequence with less total similarity is chosen as more random.\n\n**Model:** for each sequence, `compute_features` counts what share of each example type sits at each mismatch count (0–8). Inside the model, those shares are weighted by the exponential falloff. That leaves five parameters:\n- how steeply similarity falls per mismatching flip\n- how strongly alternation examples are remembered, relative to streaks\n- the same for the repeated patterns\n- the baseline level\n- how strongly the randomness difference drives the choice\n\nIt targets two discrepancies in the critique:\n- **Perfect alternation:** people choose perfectly alternating sequences less often than the best model predicts. Here alternation is an example in its own right, with its own fitted weight.\n- **Heads/tails balance:** people weight balance more than the best model implies. Similarity to the all-heads and all-tails examples falls with how balanced a sequence is, so streak examples penalise lopsided sequences directly.\n\nThe three files are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_1/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2907,"cache_read_input_tokens":58078,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2907,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"095ea2ce-fedd-436d-b76b-48f2b2b23aa3","uuid":"e71a80ec-dcaa-4c1e-92a8-f1044edb2c9d","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:01:34.756Z","request_id":"req_011CfhsW2rY4gMpqb6Vq6bPk"}
